      "text": "The sweeping claim that this beautiful African Island was uninhabited at the advent of foreign imperial invasion perfectly suits the narrative that the African native was less than human before their encounter with the rest of the world. In other words, our presence didn't count until we were enslaved by the imperial genocidaires. This is the same school of thought which contends that Egypt, Ethiopia, and the other countries in the north of the continent, including the magnificent contributions they made to enhance human progress, are not part of African history. How pathetic!",
