      "text": "The armies in most of Africa were formed by the imperial powers that were the colonial powers at the time, and those countries continue to pull the strings from behind the scenes in a system called NEOCOLONIALISM. Most of Africa was devastated by the colonial powers, who, in typical imperial fashion, shipped in people from different parts of the world that were under their sovereign control to work on their plantations, particularly in different African countries. It is common imperialist arrogance to always ignore the contribution of people of African heritage. What a colonial narrative this has been! It is a disgrace for any African to listen to this report. It goes in the same direction, which implies that Christopher Columbus discovered America, although there were people of Asian and African descent living there. DISGRACE!",
